# Review routing for this SDK.
#
# EVERY SDK BELONGS TO BESO, and that is a standing rule rather than this repo's preference:
# "Every SDK belongs to Beso — all of them, client and server. This covers the code, the CI, the
# release workflows AND the docs. Do not send an SDK PR to Roman because it is 'engineering'; the
# general department routing does not apply here."
#
# This file said `* @romchik2612`, which quietly overrode that. GitHub re-requests from CODEOWNERS
# on every push, so removing Roman by hand on a PR did nothing — he was re-added within seconds,
# and the routing rule was unenforceable from the PR side. Fixed at the source.
*                       @beska0013

# The vendored delivery substrate from mixpanel-android. Review these as provenance —
# confirm they match upstream and that the Apache 2.0 change notices are intact — rather
# than line by line. Roman stays on these: provenance review is the one thing here that is
# about the Android platform rather than about the SDK surface.
/app/src/main/java/com/intempt/core/queue/   @beska0013 @romchik2612

# Licensing and anything that ships legal text inside the artifact.
/LICENSE                @beska0013
/NOTICE                 @beska0013
